---
import Lecture from '../../../layouts/Lecture.astro';
import CodePlayground from '../../../components/CodePlayground.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/Callout.astro';
---

<Lecture
  chapterSlug="02-conditionals"
  lessonSlug="04-tax-bracket"
  hook="Combines every Chapter 2 skill in a problem you'd actually solve at a job. Marginal tax brackets — same shape as shipping tiers, volume discounts, and any tiered pricing."
>
  <h2>The brackets (simplified 2024 single-filer)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>$0 – $11,600</code> → 10%</li>
    <li><code>$11,600 – $47,150</code> → 12%</li>
    <li><code>$47,150 – $100,525</code> → 22%</li>
    <li><code>$100,525 – $191,950</code> → 24%</li>
    <li>above <code>$191,950</code> → 32%</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout tone="warning" title="🔒 no_paste mode is ON">
    <p>
      This is a graded homework. The IDE blocks paste in the entry file —
      type it out yourself. The AI Tutor will help with the <em>shape</em>
      (max hint level = 2) but won't give you the answer.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Worked trace — income = $25,000</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>First $11,600 at 10% → $1,160.00</li>
    <li>Remaining $13,400 at 12% → $1,608.00</li>
    <li><strong>Total: $2,768.00</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Pattern: start from the prior buckets, then add the partial</h2>
  <CodePlayground
    caption="Sketch of the pattern (not the full solution)"
    code={`def income_tax(income):
    if income <= 11_600:
        total = income * 0.10
    elif income <= 47_150:
        # First bracket fully consumed (1160) + 12% of the rest in this bracket
        total = 1_160 + (income - 11_600) * 0.12
    elif income <= 100_525:
        # Add the next full bracket and the partial 22% one
        total = 1_160 + 35_550 * 0.12 + (income - 47_150) * 0.22
    # ... continue for the 24% and 32% brackets ...
    else:
        total = 0  # replace with your formula
    return round(total, 2)

print(f"\${income_tax(25_000):,.2f}")    # → 2768.00`}
  />

  <h2>Acceptance criteria</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All 8 tests pass (target ≥ 7/8 per <code>tests_pass_required</code>)</li>
    <li><code>income_tax(...)</code> returns a <code>float</code></li>
    <li>All values rounded to 2 decimal places (<code>round(total, 2)</code>)</li>
    <li>No loops, no extra imports, no extra functions — Ch. 2 toolset only</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you find yourself wanting the full answer…</h2>
  <p>
    Re-do the <strong>BMI Category</strong> exercise. This homework is
    structurally the same problem with extra brackets and arithmetic. The
    "wanting the answer" feeling is a signal to slow down and re-engage with
    the simpler version.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="tip" title="Why this matters">
    <p>
      The exact same shape shows up in shipping cost tiers, volume-discount
      pricing, letter grade → GPA conversion, and game difficulty scaling. If
      you can write this homework, you can write any of those.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</Lecture>
